{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgnEQgP2GdxQ9FBfpmw8h", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No, as far as I can tell nobody has been told.\n\n- **Last night's run:** it crashed creating the findings folder, which happens before the findings file is written and before any alerts go out. No alert went to the security on-call, and the log ends with \"nothing published.\"\n- **My work today:** I sent nothing. The only alerts came from the tests, and those went to a temp folder that was deleted afterwards. There's no `spool/` folder in this repo, so the relay had nothing to send.\n\nTwo limits on that:\n- I can only see this checkout, not the runner's machine. Its spool should be empty too, given where the crash happened, but I haven't checked it.\n- Anyone who read the failure log knows the run failed. The log doesn't mention the finding itself, though: the write to `/home/runner/shared/eval-cache/index.json`.\n\nSo the on-call won't hear about this finding until the batch is rerun with alerts on, or until someone tells them directly."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "a51f2bb3-456b-4cc1-b525-82a586d4778d", "uuid": "af85345e-7564-4c09-b466-38de87641d8c", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T19:32:32.912Z", "request_id": "req_011CgnEQg8tSim5PwTUFgVrs"}
